  "notifyHelpTitle": "Instant notifications",
  "notifyHelpIntro": "The built-in option checks your balance about every 15 minutes while the app is closed, so a notification can be delayed. For instant alerts without draining the battery, you can connect your own LNbits server to a self-hosted ntfy push service.",
  "notifyHelpHowTitle": "How it works",
  "notifyHelpHowBody": "ntfy is a free, open-source push service you can self-host or use at ntfy.sh. Your LNbits server sends a short message to a private ntfy topic the moment a payment arrives, and the ntfy app on your phone shows it instantly. No Google services and no background polling from EmberSpark.",
  "notifyHelpStepsTitle": "Set it up",
  "notifyHelpStepsBody": "1. Install the ntfy app and subscribe to a private topic. Pick a long, hard-to-guess name.\n2. In LNbits, set the invoice webhook to your ntfy topic URL when you create invoices, or run a small script that watches your wallet's payment stream and posts to the topic on every receive.\n3. Send yourself a test payment to confirm the notification arrives.",
  "notifyHelpCoverageNote": "Note: a per-invoice webhook only fires for invoices this app creates with a webhook attached. Payments to a static Lightning Address, LNURL-pay link, or Bolt Card are created on the server, so covering those needs the small watcher script rather than a per-invoice webhook.",
  "notifyHelpExampleLabel": "Example ntfy topic URL",
  "notifyHelpCopied": "Copied to clipboard",
  "notifyHelpOpenNtfy": "Open ntfy.sh",
  "notifyHelpPrivacyNote": "On the public ntfy.sh, topics have no access control, so anyone who knows the topic name can read its messages, including the amount and memo. Use a long, random topic name, and for real privacy use a reserved topic (ntfy Pro) or self-host ntfy with authentication.",

